<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haguenau Forest</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Haguenau Forest is one of the largest forests in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, covering about 190 square kilometres in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> around the town of Haguenau. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> emperors used it as a hunting ground from their castle at Haguenau, and it was long called the Holy Forest because of the hermits and monasteries within it.</p></div>
